Q.1 Write the full form and one-line use of: HTTP, HTTPS, FTP, SMTP.
    HTTP — HyperText Transfer Protocol: Used to transfer web pages and data between a client and a web server.
    HTTPS — HyperText Transfer Protocol Secure: Used to securely transfer data between a client and a web server using encryption.
    FTP — File Transfer Protocol: Used to upload and download files between computers over a network.
    SMTP — Simple Mail Transfer Protocol: Used to send emails from a mail client to a mail server and between mail servers.

Q.2 What is the difference between IPv4 and IPv6?
    IPv4 uses 32-bit addresses, such as 192.168.1.1, while IPv6 uses 128-bit addresses, such as 2001:db8::1.
    IPv6 provides a much larger address space and was developed to overcome the shortage of IPv4 addresses.

